  Method: the three UDP flows differ ONLY in their Ethernet destination and use
  three different UDP ports so they are separable in one capture. The CONTROL
  must never arrive -- if it did, the switch would be flooding rather than
  routing and the subject's arrival would mean nothing. The INSTRUMENT must
  always arrive, whatever VRRP is doing, because it is addressed to the DUT's own
  permanent SVI MAC; it is what makes a zero on the subject a measurement instead
  of a dead capture. Every counted leg used identical arguments but for `--tag`:

    tools/tb sudotool tb277 ckt1406d arpleg --tag <V> \
      --out /tmp/ckt1406d/T47873 --iface eth3 --watch eth4 \
      --sender-ip 10.38.22.33 --gw-mac e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 \
      --arp 10.38.22.36 \
      --udp '10.38.22.65:9999%00:00:5e:00:01:0a,
             10.38.22.65:9998%02:00:00:00:00:99,
             10.38.22.65:9997%e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43' \
      --count 5 --show-ttl

